{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of Lovász's (g,f)-factor theorem (1970): for a finite simple graph G and g ≤ f : V → ℕ, G has a spanning subgraph H with g(v) ≤ deg_H(v) ≤ f(v) for every vertex if and only if, for all disjoint vertex sets S and T, h(S,T) ≤ Σ_{v∈S} f(v) + Σ_{v∈T} (deg_{G−S}(v) − g(v)), where h(S,T) is the number of components C of G − (S ∪ T) with g = f on C and Σ_{v∈C} f(v) + e(C,T) odd (lovasz_gf_factor). As a corollary, the criterion of Heinrich, Hell, Kirkpatrick and Liu for g < f, without the component term (gf_factor_of_lt). The proof reduces the theorem to Tutte's f-factor theorem, imported as a lake dependency from PALOMAR-2026-10-18-000005, through a gadget: f(v) − g(v) slack vertices are joined to each vertex v, and the slack vertices together with one extra vertex form a clique, with target degree 1 on slack vertices and (Σ g) mod 2 on the extra vertex. One definition beyond Mathlib's (h(S,T), tightOddCount); g and f are natural-number valued.",
